  "worked_solution": "If the energy consumption of an average household is $E\\,\\text{kWh},$ then the rate of change of the energy consumption is $\\frac{\\text{d}E}{\\text{d}t},$ where $t$ is the time in weeks.\n\nSince an additional $1\\,\\text{kWh}$ is consumed every week, the rate of change of the energy consumption is given by the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}E}{\\text{d}t}=1.\n$$",
